  "_about": "Which painted image draws each asset. tools/art.py turns the art release zips into img/ from this file. Each pool entry is one look, picked by the asset's seed; its keys are states, each a stem whose -day, -dusk and -night files are the lights (a stem with no light suffix is used at every hour). A state with no stem keeps the idle image; idle with no image keeps the coded art. fit: the box side the idle image is scaled to (h height, w width). flip: the image faces left. rot: degrees to turn it. skip: stem-light files left out (a halo or a real landmark). slots: where carried things stand, as fractions of the drawn width and height from the anchor.",
